Hi team,
 I=E2=80=99ve spent the last few months diving deep into our share group me=
chanics, specifically focusing on distributed acknowledgements, fault toler=
ance, and recovery protocols. To move us forward, I=E2=80=99ve mapped out a=
 detailed design and architectural diagrams=C2=A0=C2=A0here:=C2=A0https://d=
ocs.google.com/document/d/1sWMZ1c3j_rwg1jQByZ4rW-66GGoswkRI3DnSUiJPJ94/edit=
?tab=3Dt.0=C2=A0

Public APIs and High level overview KIP:=C2=A0https://cwiki.apache.org/conf=
luence/x/J448G=C2=A0
Please review the proposals so we can align on the implementation details.=
=C2=A0 Next, I will outline the integration plan with Flink to support queu=
e semantics (as a proof that our KIP changes will going to help stream proc=
essing engines like Flink) where consumer elasticity matters more than thro=
ughput, and topics with severe partition skew.
Regards,Shekhar Rajak=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0  =20
