Yuriy Badalyantc created KAFKA-20892:
----------------------------------------

             Summary: SimpleHeaderConverter infers a string header as a number if it starts with a digit
                 Key: KAFKA-20892
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20892
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: connect
    Affects Versions: 4.3.1
            Reporter: Yuriy Badalyantc
            Assignee: Yuriy Badalyantc


When `SimpleHeaderConverter` tries to decode a header with value like this: `1::2`, it mistakenly infers the type of the value as number and returns `1` as a result of decoding.

The reason is in the `Values.parseString` implementation. There was a [ticket|https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-9083] to fix a number of similar parsing problems, but this particular problem was not included.



