Hi Jun,

Thanks for the comments.
Answering them below.

> JR36. Sounds good. Should we remove MirrorLeaderEpochExceededException?

Sorry, it=E2=80=99s a confusing name. The MirrorLeaderEpochExceededExceptio=
n is
used and thrown when the fetched mirror batch leader epoch > local leader
epoch in destination cluster. And then we=E2=80=99ll stop mirroring and mov=
e the
partition to EPOCH_FENSING state to wait for local leader epoch bump. I
think since we don=E2=80=99t have the concept of `MirrorLeaderEpoch` anymor=
e, the
`MirrorLeaderEpochExceededException` should not cause confusion now. I=E2=
=80=99ll
keep the name for the exception.


> JR51. Sounds good. Do we plan to always set lastFetchedEpoch in the mirro=
r
fetch request issued to the source cluster, independent of the value of
mirror.support.unclean.leader.election? It's needed to detect divergence
during failover. However, if it's also set when
mirror.support.unclean.leader.election=3Dfalse,
an unclean leader election in the source cluster can halt the mirroring
since we don=E2=80=99t do anything with the returned divergeEpoch in that m=
ode
and continue
the next fetch.

> Do we plan to always set lastFetchedEpoch in the mirror
fetch request issued to the source cluster, independent of the value of
Mirror.support.unclean.leader.election?

Yes, we always set lastFetchedEpoch in the mirror fetch request.

> However, if it's also set when
mirror.support.unclean.leader.election=3Dfalse,
an unclean leader election in the source cluster can halt the mirroring
since we don=E2=80=99t do anything with the returned divergeEpoch in that m=
ode
and continue the next fetch.

Sorry I didn=E2=80=99t make it clear. When
=E2=80=9Cmirror.support.unclean.leader.election=3Dfalse=E2=80=9D and a =E2=
=80=9CdivergeEpoch=E2=80=9D is set
in fetch response, the leader node will handle the divergeEpoch and then
continue the next fetch as usual. The difference with
=E2=80=9Cmirror.support.unclean.leader.election=3Dtrue=E2=80=9D is that =E2=
=80=9Cshould we wait for
ALL replicas caught up (complete truncation)=E2=80=9D. Without the waiting,=
 it=E2=80=99s
possible the inconsistent log issue in KAFKA-18723 could happen between
leader and follower nodes in the destination cluster because we don=E2=80=
