Xi Wang created KAFKA-20917:
-------------------------------

             Summary: Improve RecordAccumulator.ready performance
                 Key: KAFKA-20917
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20917
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
          Components: producer=20
            Reporter: Xi Wang
         Attachments: Screenshot 2026-08-10 at 8.37.01=E2=80=AFPM.png, Scre=
enshot 2026-08-10 at 8.42.36=E2=80=AFPM.png, Screenshot 2026-08-10 at 8.45.=
57=E2=80=AFPM.png, image-2026-08-10-20-35-09-732.png, image-2026-08-10-20-4=
3-01-781.png

After upgrading producer client from 2.9 to 3.9, we noticed produce latency=
 increase, especially for ack-all producer, e.g. P50 latency increase from =
8ms to 13ms, ~60% increase.=C2=A0
!Screenshot 2026-08-10 at 8.37.01=E2=80=AFPM.png!

The profiling shows partitionReady call is hot.=C2=A0

!image-2026-08-10-20-35-09-732.png!
The 3.9 client include many checks and calculations in RecordAccumulator.re=
ady -> partitionReady method, especially for adaptive partitioning. after d=
isable adaptive partitioning, we still didn't see latency drop to as 2.9 cl=
ient.=C2=A0
2.9 client profiling
!Screenshot 2026-08-10 at 8.42.36=E2=80=AFPM.png!
3.9 client profiling
!image-2026-08-10-20-43-01-781.png!



We found out the linked PRs address performance issue and after deploying i=
t to our ack-all cluster (with adaptive partitioning disabled), the latency=
 became similar as 2.9 client.

!Screenshot 2026-08-10 at 8.45.57=E2=80=AFPM.png!

=C2=A0



