Hi Jun,

Thanks for the good comments,
Answering them below.

> JR80. PauseMirrorTopicsOptions: "PauseMirrorTopics/ResumeMirrorTopics
supports regex in the ClusterMirrorComamnd, but we don=E2=80=99t need to ad=
d the
=E2=80=9Cpatterns=E2=80=9D."
So, in this case, we use topics to support both specific topics and regex.
However, startMirrorTopicsOptions uses topics for specific topics and
includePatterns for regex. Could we make them consistent?


The purpose of the =E2=80=9CincludePatterns=E2=80=9D field is for the
=E2=80=9Cmirror.topics.include=E2=80=9D update, so that if there is any new=
ly created topic
in the source cluster that matches the regex, we can create it. And the
=E2=80=9CTopics=E2=80=9D field in the StartMirrorTopicsRequest is to specif=
y the topicId
and numPartitions in the source cluster. So I think =E2=80=9CincludePattern=
s=E2=80=9D and
=E2=80=9CTopics=E2=80=9D both are necessary in the StartMirrorTopicsRequest=
. On the other
hand, in PauseMirrorTopics, because it won=E2=80=99t change the
=E2=80=9Cmirror.topics.include=E2=80=9D/=E2=80=9Dmirror.topics.exclude=E2=
=80=9D configs, we don=E2=80=99t need to
provide the regex in the request.



> JR82. DescribeClusterMirrorsResponse.SourceOffset: Is the value also -1 i=
f
it's not included in the request?

If =E2=80=9CIncludeMirrorOffset=E2=80=9D is disabled, we won=E2=80=99t quer=
y the mirror partition
leader, so we can=E2=80=99t get the sourceOffset.

I assume you want to ask `if it=E2=80=99s still -1 if not actively mirrorin=
g, while
=E2=80=9CIncludeMirrorOffset=E2=80=9D is enabled`. That=E2=80=99s a good qu=
estion. I think our
purpose of this command is to show the lag to users. So if the state is not
MIRRORING (ex: STOPPED/PAUSED), we think it=E2=80=99s not helpful to users =
to show
only the sourceOffset. Of course users can use `kafka-get-offsets.sh` to
get the offset if they really want to know.


> JR83. Start Mirror Topics:
> JR83.1 Should the controller verify the expected state for the topic?

As replied in JR84, the desired state validation should happen in the
broker. And the controller validates the StateOffset. I=E2=80=99ve updated =
the
workflow to make it clear.

> JR83.2 "d. truncates the log accordingly,"
Could you add a description of the truncation offset?

OK, added one more sentence:
d. based on the last mirror epoch response in (b), the broker translates
the epoch into the offset by querying the leaderEpochCache
(endOffsetForEpoch), and truncates the log accordingly, and waits for all
ISR members=E2=80=A6


> JR84. Stop Mirror Topics: "The controller verifies that the desired state
of all topics are in MIRRORING or PAUSED state."
Should the broker verfy the topic level state? I thought the controller
will use StateOffset in the request to make sure the validation on the
broker is stil valid. If the controller performs the verification, is
StateOffset still useful?

Oh, you=E2=80=99re right. We=E2=80=99re doing duplicated work here. Yes, th=
e broker already
verifies the =E2=80=9Cdesired state=E2=80=9D of all topics are in MIRRORING=
 or PAUSED
state, as well as the =E2=80=9Cactual state=E2=80=9D is in MIRRORING or PAU=
SED state. If
all validation passes, we=E2=80=99ll forward it to the controller. So the
controller only needs to validate the StateOffset to make sure the
validation on the broker is still valid. So, yes, we don=E2=80=99t need the=
 desired
state validation on the controller side. I=E2=80=99ve updated the KIP to ma=
ke it
clear.

One more thing to add is that, I=E2=80=99ve thought about not adding StateO=
ffset,
and relying on the desired state validation to make sure we=E2=80=99re safe=
 to do
the deletion or other operations. The problem is that, even if the broker
sees the desired state for topic A is STOPPED, and then the controller also
sees the desired state is STOPPED, it still cannot make sure the
controller=E2=80=99s STOPPED state equals the broker=E2=80=99s STOPPED stat=
e. For example:
1. Broker sees STOPPED, then forward to controller
2. User changes the desired state to MIRRORING
3. User changes the desired state to STOPPED
4. Controller sees the desired state is STOPPED
So I think StateOffset is required.

Thanks for catching it BTW.


> JR85. There are still a few references to includeMirrorLags. They should
be
IncludeMirrorOffset.

Sorry, just updated.


> JR86. Metrics:
> JR86.1 Could you describe the type (gauge, meter, etc) of each metric?

KIP is updated. I also group the metrics into new added metrics and other
inherited metrics.

> JR86.2 Could you describe a bit more what MinFetchRate represents?

It means the lowest fetch request rate among all of this mirror fetcher
manager's fetcher threads. It inherits from the AbstractFetcherManager=E2=
=80=99s
metric.


> JR87. Version Compatibility: "For migration or DR use cases where failbac=
k
is not required, this proposal supports source brokers up to version 2.1
included"
This KIP needs topicId and KIP-516 was introduced later than 2.1.
Yes, when mirroring from a cluster without topic id support, we will assign
a random topic ID in the destination cluster and then fetch (without topic
id in the fetch request using the old version of Fetch API) as usual. Of
course this is for the one-way mirroring use case. It can=E2=80=99t start t=
he
reverse mirror(failback) under this setup. You can check the =E2=80=9CCompa=
tibility
Matrix=E2=80=9D section for more detail.


Thank you,
Luke

