Hi Luke,

I understand your point, but the only plausible solution that completely
eliminates the risk would be a one-size-fits-all mechanism that safely
calculates retention.ms automatically for every cluster. In reality, it is
impossible for the system to do a better job of determining whether a piece
of metadata is still needed than the operators themselves, who have far
more context and information about their workloads and topic configurations=
.

I don't think this is a problem that can be solved at the system level, as
it ultimately relies on the operator's operational knowledge.

In fact, if there is such good dynamic mechanism to calculate an
appropriate retention.ms, then maybe that=E2=80=99s the ideal solution for =
limiting
the size of the metadata topic, instead of the compacting solution itself.
But if you have any good idea on that, I would love to hear your thoughts.


Best,
Lijun Tong

