Content-Type: text/plain; charset="us-ascii"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

Hi all,

I'd like to start a discussion on KIP-1372, which proposes rejecting
topic creation and topic-level config changes that would set
min.insync.replicas above the topic's replication factor, instead of
silently accepting a configuration that can never satisfy acks=3Dall
(KAFKA-19726, and KAFKA-4680 from 2017).

KIP: https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/spaces/KAFKA/pages/449286526/KIP-1=
372+Reject+topic+configurations+where+min.insync.replicas+exceeds+the+repli=
cation+factor

This revisits ground covered by KIP-579 (2020, never adopted); the KIP
explains why KIP-966's effective-min-ISR clamp changes that analysis.

Feedback welcome.

Gavin

--_000_YQBPR0101MB46038B535810E27CD5AC758EDFAD2YQBPR0101MB4603_--

