Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21008) Consider allowing record headers to
 be filtered or masked before persistence in Kafka Streams state stores
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "sanghyeok An (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

sanghyeok An created KAFKA-21008:
------------------------------------

             Summary: Consider allowing record headers to be filtered or ma=
sked before persistence in Kafka Streams state stores
                 Key: KAFKA-21008
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21008
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: sanghyeok An
            Assignee: sanghyeok An


Kafka Streams header-aware state stores introduced by KIP-1271 can persist =
record headers together with state values and propagate them through state=
=C2=A0store changelogs.

=C2=A0

Record headers may contain application-level sensitive information, such as=
=C2=A0credentials, tokens, personally identifiable information, or request =
metadata=C2=A0that should not be retained at rest.

=C2=A0

Currently, Kafka Streams does not provide a built-in mechanism to filter,=
=C2=A0remove, or mask selected headers before they are written to a header-=
aware=C2=A0state store. Applications must sanitize headers manually before =
every=C2=A0stateful operator, which is error-prone and may also modify the =
headers=C2=A0observed by downstream processors.

=C2=A0

Kafka Streams should provide an opt-in mechanism to filter or transform the=
=C2=A0copy of the headers that is persisted by header-aware state stores.

=C2=A0

The mechanism should:
 *  Allow selected headers to be removed or their values to be masked.
 * Apply consistently to both local state and state-store changelog records=
.
 * Avoid mutating the headers of the in-flight input record.
 * Preserve the current behavior when no filtering or masking policy is con=
figured.
 * Ensure that restored state contains the same sanitized headers that were=
=C2=A0written to the local store.



