sanghyeok An created KAFKA-21009:
------------------------------------

             Summary: Consider introducing record header handling policies =
for Kafka Streams stateful operations
                 Key: KAFKA-21009
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21009
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: sanghyeok An
            Assignee: sanghyeok An


Stateful operations such as joins and aggregations may combine or retain re=
cords from multiple inputs. Unlike one-to-one stateless=C2=A0operations, th=
ere may not be an obvious set of headers to use for the output record.

=C2=A0

Currently, header handling is determined by the behavior of each operator, =
and applications do not have an explicit policy for=C2=A0controlling it.

=C2=A0

We should consider whether Kafka Streams stateful operations could support =
header handling policies such as:
 * Retaining the existing behavior
 * Ignoring or dropping headers
 * Preserving headers from a selected input record
 * Merging headers from multiple input records

This Jira is intended to capture the use case and evaluate whether such pol=
icies would be useful. If pursued, the affected=C2=A0operators, exact polic=
y set, defaults, conflict handling, and consistency across caching and rest=
oration should be defined through=C2=A0a KIP.



